     The original implementation required level 15 (probably
because it was half way to 30 rather than being based on
whether it was a reasonable level to attain or necessary to
have a good chance to successfully complete the quest).  I
lobbied to reduce that, because 15 does take too much effort
to reach.  Even level 14 is higher than necessary for some
roles, but level 14 is one of the levels where rank title
changes (from Magician to Enchanter/Enchantress as a wizard,
for instance).  So it was picked in order to allow quest
messages to use the title instead of an arbitrary number--or
simply being vague--when telling the player to gain further
experience.


